    <briefdescription>
<para>File and I/O operation errors. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classcslt_1_1IOError" kindref="compound">IOError</ref> represents errors related to file operations, reading, writing, permissions, timeouts, and other I/O operations.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example Usage:</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Using<sp/>default<sp/>message</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>IOError();<sp/><sp/>//<sp/>&quot;I/O<sp/>operation<sp/>failed&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Using<sp/>custom<sp/>message</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>IOError(&quot;Failed<sp/>to<sp/>open<sp/>file:<sp/>config.txt&quot;);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
